    <briefdescription>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Data structure for dynamic typing of int, bigint, and double</para>
<para>Using this union allows to store any of the supported data types in the same container and allows to &quot;see&quot; its current type. <verbatim>embed:rst

**Usage:**

.. code-block:: c++
   :caption: To store data in multitype array:

   multitype m[5];
   int    foo = 1;
   double bar = 2.5;
   bigint baz = 1&lt;&lt;40 - 1;
   m[0] = foo;
   m[1] = bar;
   m[2] = -1;
   m[3] = 2.0;
   m[4] = baz;

.. code-block:: c++
   :caption: To format data from multitype array into a space separated string:

   std::string str;
   for (int i = 0; i &lt; 5; ++i) {
       switch (m[i].type) {
           case multitype::DOUBLE:
               str += std::to_string(m[i].data.d) + &apos; &apos;;
               break;
           case multitype::INT:
               str += std::to_string(m[i].data.i) + &apos; &apos;;
               break;
           case multitype::BIGINT:
               str += std::to_string(m[i].data.b) + &apos; &apos;;
               break;
           default:
               break;
       }
   }
</verbatim> </para>
    </detaileddescription>
